                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_input" index="10">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The shape of the inflow. Log law (Richards &amp; Hoxey): OpenFOAM's atmBoundaryLayer inlet, k constant with height — the default and what every earlier study used. Harris &amp; Deaves (ESDU 01008): the strong-wind boundary layer of the UK National Annex to EN 1991-1-4, which the City of London Wind Microclimate Guidelines (2019) require — a gradient-height term on the mean speed and the measured strong-wind turbulence, written as fixedProfile tables for U, k (3/2·σu², so the gust Eddy3D reads from k is the Harris &amp; Deaves gust) and epsilon. Each direction gets its own table from its own speed and z0. Either way the cases sample the profile approaching the model, so the Study Report plots simulated against target (as the guideline asks) and scores the ASCE CWE prestandard's ABL self-sustainment check (AC 5-9) on it.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">71e09844-cc2c-4fd7-8289-a51a64467875</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Inlet Profile</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Profile</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="Options" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Log law (Richards &amp; Hoxey)
Harris &amp; Deaves (ESDU 01008)</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="Value" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Log law (Richards &amp; Hoxey)</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="2">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
