                    <chunk name="param_input" index="21">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">What the mesh's own checkMesh verdict does to the numerics before Simulate. checkMesh runs as the last step of Mesh; Simulate reads its 06_checkMesh.txt (after checking it describes the mesh on disk) and presets the numerics PATH: 'auto' (default) — a failed check, or max skewness &gt; 4 / non-orthogonality &gt; 70° (checkMesh's own limits) solves on the 'robust' path (p 0.3 / U 0.5 / turbulence 0.25, three correctors, a longer warm-up); skewness ≥ 10, non-orthogonality ≥ 80° or inverted cells on 'hardened' (that path plus a potentialFoam start and a doubled warm-up). A mesh that passes changes nothing. 'off' keeps the Numerics above whatever the mesh looks like; 'robust' / 'hardened' apply that preset unconditionally. The convection, gradient and laplacian schemes and the convergence criterion are never touched, so the answer is the one the Numerics input asks for — only the route to it moves. Run All applies it too: unless this is 'off' it meshes in its own window and opens Simulate once the new mesh is built and checked. The Wind Run component says what was applied. Optional.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">07f00a4a-d83d-45fc-8c1f-b55ea2dc9145</item>
