                    <chunk name="param_input" index="22">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The study's pedestrian (comfort sampling) height above ground, m. Where Pedestrian Average samples, and recorded in the case (controlDict marker + eddy3d-study.json) so Study Report can print it and check it against an authority — the City of London guideline asks for 1.5 m — and ParaView's pedestrian slice follows it. Default 1.75 m, the value used before this was a setting, so existing studies are unchanged. It declares the height; place your probe points at it.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c78d97af-14e5-467b-8309-93918df4dc36</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Pedestrian Height</item>
