                    <chunk name="param_input" index="23">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The planning guideline this study is set up for. City of London (2019): SETS the pedestrian height to 1.5 m (unless Pedestrian Height is wired or changed) and prism layers that put three cells below 1.5 m (absolute sizes: 0.3 m first layer, ratio 1.2); RECORDS itself, so Study Report checks against it without its Authority input; and WARNS — on this component and on Outdoor Case — about what it cannot set for you: 36 directions at 10°, 400 m of modelled context, the Harris &amp; Deaves inlet (ABL → Inlet Profile), cell sizes, a turbulence model it advises against. None (the default) changes nothing.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">da78741e-dbd4-4bac-972e-2b9edc84d1d2</item>
